   "lines": [
    [
     "c10_1",
     {
      "label": "hook",
      "head": "How an *electric car* works",
      "pose": "point",
      "face": "grin",
      "prop": {
       "type": "ev"
      }
     },
     "No pistons, no gearbox full of gears, no exhaust. So how does an electric car work?"
    ],
    [
     "c10_2",
     {
      "label": "battery",
      "head": "A huge *battery* in the floor",
      "pose": "present",
      "face": "smile",
      "prop": {
       "type": "ev"
      }
     },
     "Hundreds or even thousands of cells sit in a flat pack under the floor, storing energy as direct current."
    ],
    [
     "c10_3",
     {
      "label": "inverter",
      "head": "The *inverter* is the brain",
      "pose": "count",
      "face": "smug",
      "prop": {
       "type": "ev"
      }
     },
     "The inverter turns that DC into alternating current for the motor, and controls exactly how fast it spins."
    ],
    [
     "c10_4",
     {
      "label": "motor",
      "head": "The *motor* pushes with magnets",
      "pose": "cheer",
      "face": "wow",
      "prop": {
       "type": "ev"
      }
     },
     "Inside the motor, magnetic fields push and pull the rotor around. Full pulling power from zero rpm."
    ],
    [
     "c10_5",
     {
      "label": "regen",
      "head": "Braking *makes* electricity",
      "pose": "present",
      "face": "happy",
      "prop": {
       "type": "ev",
       "regen": true
      }
     },
     "When you lift off, the motor works in reverse as a generator, slowing the car and sending energy back to the battery."
    ],
    [
     "c10_6",
     {
      "label": "maintenance",
      "head": "Far *fewer* parts to service",
      "pose": "thumbs",
      "face": "grin",
      "prop": {
       "type": "checklist",
       "items": [
        [
         "Oil changes",
         false
        ],
        [
         "Spark plugs",
         false
        ],
        [
         "Exhaust system",
         false
        ]
       ]
      }
     },
     "No oil changes, no spark plugs, no clutch, no exhaust. Far fewer moving parts to wear out."
    ],
    [
     "c10_7",
     {
      "label": "still",
      "head": "Tyres and brakes still *matter*",
      "pose": "shrug",
      "face": "smug",
      "prop": {
       "type": "tags",
       "items": [
